{
  "description": "One table of cases for every HotLayout reader (schema 9.17.0): a list item \u2014 \u00abText.marker\u00bb. Rules: x-style.layout.listMarker. Numbers are logical pixels. \u00abfontSize\u00bb is the font size of the BASE style of the text of the node with the system text scale already applied; \u00abgroupSize\u00bb is the number of items of the group of a numbered item BY THE DOCUMENT (for a bullet it is not read). \u00abgeometryCases\u00bb: the column of the marker, the gap and the hanging indent (column + gap). \u00abtextCases\u00bb: what the marker says. \u00abnumberCases\u00bb: \u00absiblings\u00bb are the children of ONE parent in the order of the document \u2014 \u00abtype\u00bb, \u00abmarker\u00bb (absent \u2014 no field) and \u00abvisible: false\u00bb for a node hidden by its condition; \u00abexpect.numbers[i]\u00bb is the number the i-th sibling is drawn with (for a hidden numbered item \u2014 the number it would have if it became visible; null \u2014 not a numbered item), \u00abexpect.groupSizes[i]\u00bb \u2014 the size of its group. \u00abinstanceCases\u00bb: a numbered item that is the template of a data list \u2014 one entry of \u00abtemplateVisible\u00bb per drawn record. \u00ablayoutCases\u00bb: a node of the width \u00abplaceInline\u00bb; boxes are spans along the line from the LEFT edge of the node; \u00ablines\u00bb is how many lines the text took in its column (given), \u00ablineBlock\u00bb the pitch of a line. \u00abnaturalCases\u00bb: the width an item wants in a row. A row marked \u00abreaderOnly\u00bb is a document the builder never produces.",
